    "done_when": "a-dispatch-returns-without-its-worker §4's done-when holds. The launch-kind table in skills/reckon-build/SKILL.md says a CLI dispatch returns once its supervisor is running, without waiting for the worker to be spawned, and is run in the foreground. That row claims no order between the dispatch's exit and the spawn. skills/reckon-build/references/orchestrator-harness/claude-code.md names the follower as the session's only monitor. The scout note in skills/reckon-build/references/sprint-orchestration.md and the line in skills/reckon-build/references/worker-backends.md that backgrounds a CLI dispatch and yields are rewritten: a scout is still dispatched first and not waited on, but the dispatch command runs in the foreground. The manifest lists every line that grep -rn \"dispatch\" skills/ returns that mentions backgrounding, read line by line, and names any such line in a file outside the four write paths as a follow-on. tests/test_skill_contracts.py passes at head, and any skill test that pins those files passes too, each named in the manifest. Every log sits under the run directory, headed with revision, tree and literal command, and ends EXIT=. Only skills/reckon-build/SKILL.md, skills/reckon-build/references/orchestrator-harness/claude-code.md, skills/reckon-build/references/sprint-orchestration.md and skills/reckon-build/references/worker-backends.md change.",
